  "goodToKnow": "Die Legislaturperiode is a legislative term, officially Wahlperiode: the period between elections. The Bundestag's term is four years, while most Landtage now have five-year terms. Plans not passed by the end of a term usually lapse, a principle called Diskontinuität. Die Legislative is the legislature, alongside die Exekutive and die Judikative in the separation of powers (Gewaltenteilung). Plural: die Legislaturperioden."
